In Alice's Wonderland, solve the following problem step by step.

In the diagram below, \( AB = AC = 150 \), \( AD = 50 \), and \( CF = 100 \). Compute \( \frac{[CEF]}{[DBE]} \).

[asy]
unitsize(0.025 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F;

B = (0,0);
C = (100,0);
A = intersectionpoint(arc(B,150,0,180),arc(C,150,0,180));
D = interp(A,B,50/150);
F = interp(A,C,(150 + 100)/150);
E = extension(B,C,D,F);

draw(C--B--A--F--D);

label("$A$", A, N);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, SE);
label("$D$", D, W);
label("$E$", E, S);
label("$F$", F, SE);
[/asy]

Please put your final answer inside \boxed{}.

